#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Afterstreet shopfit pack, version 1 (26 October 2026): the architecture and materials that make a mapped business look like one: shop doors and windows, roll-up and bay doors, drop-ceiling tiles and light fittings, exposed trusses,
partitions and restroom fittings, exit signs, extinguishers, sprinklers, cameras, wainscot, column covers, and 2 m floor-material patches (checker tile, linoleum, carpets, hardwood, polished concrete, epoxy, rubber, terrazzo, quarry tile).
Writes assets/shaped/shopfit.js. Run: python3 assets/shaped/src/shopfit.py

models.shopfit.<name>: metres, origin at the centre of the base, front facing +Z. Wall pieces are 0.1 to 0.2 m deep and stand on the floor against a wall (back at -z); floor patches are 2 x 2 m decals at y = 0.02; ceiling pieces hang from y = 3.0 (their info.h is measured from 0)."""
